[3] consec gaps are 1..7 (k=8). Which pairs of consec activate a coupling?
    active pairs (|P|>0): 0
    sum over active = +0.00000000  (= corr_2(consec))

[4] INTERPRETATION (the THM-559 twin, honest):
    * corr_2 IS an exact 2-body (pairwise) energy on offsets, zero field.
    * per-pair coupling P_k(0,d) is NONZERO only when 7|d (resonant gap),
      and is NEGATIVE there.  Generic gaps give P=0.
    * consec_{k} (k<=7) has all gaps in 1..k-1<7 -> NO resonant pair ->
      corr_2=0, the 2-body GROUND STATE (max, since all couplings<=0).
    * any shape with a 7-multiple gap pays a negative 2-body penalty.
    => consec is 2-body-extremal BY A PER-PAIR ARGUMENT (provable).
    HONEST LIMIT: the 2-body layer is tiny (|corr_2|<=0.0052) and its max
    is 0; the BULK of measS7 and of consec's lead lives in the >=3-body
    layers (c3~+0.08, high-residual~+0.22 at k=8).  The cut/cycle split
    cleanly ISOLATES a provable 2-body extremal piece, but the crux is
    irreducibly many-body -- exactly THM-555's 'cycle space' verdict.
